xnu: 0183 disable proc_prepareexit call in exit1 (vince nofw2 semantic)

The hand-built nofw2 kernel NOP'd this call and the boot got past the
init_featureflags[16] exited handshake panic. Source-level equivalent
for CI builds.

--- a/bsd/kern/kern_exit.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_exit.c
@@ -1583,7 +1583,8 @@
 	proc_transend(p, 1);
 	proc_unlock(p);
 
-	proc_prepareexit(p, rv, perf_notify);
+	/* VINCE: disabled - matches the hand-built nofw2 kernel NOP. */
+	if (0) proc_prepareexit(p, rv, perf_notify);
 
 	/* Last thread to terminate will call proc_exit() */
 	task_terminate_internal(task);
